Stipple was inspired by dithercn (https://dithercn.dev), a set of dithered components for React
and shadcn by its authors, which is distributed under the MIT license. Its idea of one dither
engine under many components, themed with an ink and a paper colour, and its agent skill for
writing new dithers, shaped this project. Stipple shares no code with it and is an independent
project, not affiliated with or endorsed by dithercn.

The gallery and the docs use the Geist and Geist Mono typefaces by Vercel, distributed under the
SIL Open Font License 1.1 (https://openfontlicense.org). The fonts are bundled with the gallery
apps and loaded from @fontsource-variable in the docs.

The blue-noise texture in stipple/src/commonMain/.../internal/BlueNoiseData.kt is generated by
scripts/blue-noise.py with the void-and-cluster method, from scratch, and is not taken from
another texture set.
